@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] shared-file-icons-retain-canonical-strokes
Both hosts MUST render the existing Catppuccin XML file icons with their same path
geometry, fill and stroke colors, stroke width, caps, joins and viewport. Generation
MUST reject unsupported structures rather than omit them. File names MUST retain the
existing icon-selection precedence and fallback. Source: existing FilePath/FileIcon
behavior retained by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision; DESIGN.md rule 48.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;motion] kit-decides-the-way
Which way a page, tab, file or label moves is decided in the kit, never by a screen:
`BlurSwitch`, `LabelSwitch` and `rememberPageSlide` take an `order` and work the way out
with `pageWay`, and Back goes through `PageBack`. A kit slide MUST take its offset from
the way (rule 105; motion check).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] kit-drags-carry-on-or-settle
A page, row or sheet let go after a drag settles back where it was or carries on the way
the finger went, at the speed it was thrown; it never springs toward the start first. A
throw of 500dp/s counts as a swipe once the finger has taken the page part of the way, so
a nudge never turns a page by itself (L6, `kit-side-pages-slide-whole`), and a throw back
against the drag cancels it (rule 105).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] kit-side-pages-slide-whole
`SidePages` and `FilePages` move pages that sit side by side the whole width with
nothing fading or blurring, both pages in view while they move, and settle on
`PullsMotion.PageSpring`, critically damped with no snap at the end (rule 107; H20, H36,
J7). The Overview's pages are drawn before the first drag, so the first swipe from Summary
to Conversation moves as smoothly as the way back and never pops or holds at its start
(recording 16 Oct 09:50, 03:29 to 03:53; M8). A page moves exactly as far as the finger, and a quick flick turns the page only once
the finger has moved it part of the way, so a page never "swipes by itself" (recording
15 Oct 15:37, 04:12 to 04:31; L6).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] kit-side-pages-keep-state
A page held by `SidePages` keeps its scroll and saved state while another page is on
screen, and finds them again when it comes back (rule 118; J9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-toast-action-keeps-its-current-message
A toast action MUST run at most once and only while that exact message is current.
Its message MUST remain current during the action so the existing Undo callbacks can
check their ownership. Finishing or failing the action MUST retire only its own
message; a replacement shown by the callback MUST remain visible. Source: the
existing toast Undo behavior retained by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 same-app iOS decision,
DESIGN.md rule 73 and the shared review confirmation ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;motion] sheet-paper-comes-up-solid
A sheet's paper MUST come up opaque: only what is on it fades in through the panel
reveal's cross-blur, never the page behind showing through the panel. Its window MUST NOT
show a system dim on any frame, and the status bar icons MUST stay readable over the page
while it opens. Source: Tavi's recording of 26 Oct 2026, 01:07 to 01:28 (Settings drew
see-through and "some black thing glitches out").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] sheets-and-foot-bars-stay-column-wide
A sheet's panel and the foot bar MUST be no wider than ReadableWidth (less the bar's
margins). In an unfolded window a sheet MUST rise over the pane whose page opened it,
while its scrim still dims the whole window (rule 5). In a window under 600dp tall and
600dp or more wide, a sheet MUST rest at its tall height, and a page header MUST sit 8dp
under the status bar instead of 48dp from the top. Source: Tavi's message of 27 Oct 2026
12:55, DESIGN.md rules 207 and 208.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] markdown-quote-bar-spans-the-quote
